    "statement": "Assume full AC. Put $\\mathcal A_r=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^4:r/2<|x|<2r\\}$, with Euclidean coefficient and Frobenius matrix norms. There are universal $\\delta,C>0$ such that every smooth $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ connection form $A$ near $\\overline{\\mathcal A_r}$ with\n$$r^2\\|F_A\\|_{L^\\infty(\\mathcal A_r)}\\le\\delta$$\nhas a smooth gauge $g:\\mathcal A_r\\to SU(2)$ satisfying\n$$\\|A^g\\|_{L^\\infty(\\mathcal A_r)}\\le Cr\\|F_A\\|_{L^\\infty(\\mathcal A_r)},\\qquad A^g=g^{-1}dg+g^{-1}Ag.$$\nNo Coulomb condition or gauge bound from a curvature $L^2$ norm alone is asserted here.",
    "raw_sha256": "7d7fb2d0ee52ad0a231f53adc0094a99a8af198d6480ee9552f5b9166b08f46e"
  },
